I'm thinking about how selection updates might happen before the outline controller state updates. For example, if a selection is set to a hidden block via the controller without a widget, it becomes more complex. Hidden selections only matter within the widget. So, I can implement a feature in the widget that detects this hidden selection after controller changes and calls for outline expansion. This way, any selection type causing a hidden selection will reveal it automatically, ensuring all selection sources are handled in one spot.
